{
 "P001": {
  "title": "Fast Widget Learning",
  "abstract": "We study how quickly a widget can be learned from few examples.",
  "full_text": [
   {
    "section_name": "Introduction",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Widgets are everywhere. Many annotators and many corpus builders ask each time how labelled data is gathered for widgets, and how many papers describe it."
    ]
   },
   {
    "section_name": "Background",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Three annotators labelled each sample of the corpus and disagreements were settled by a fourth annotator."
    ]
   },
   {
    "section_name": "Method",
    "paragraphs": [
     "We use a plain pipeline.",
     "The widget encoder is trained with the Lamport optimizer, a learning rate of 0.01 and a batch size of 32."
    ]
   },
   {
    "section_name": "Results",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Accuracy rose steadily with more examples. Gains flattened after one thousand samples."
    ]
   },
   {
    "section_name": "Discussion",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Limits include small samples and noisy inputs."
    ]
   },
   {
    "section_name": "Conclusion",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Fast learning of widgets is feasible with modest compute."
    ]
   }
  ],
